    Hello,

    here comes the TuxMobil News reminder for 11/2005. You may find
    all messages in the monthly digest[2].

    Please support our work by submitting news and Linux reports about
    laptops, notebooks, PDAs, mobile phones and portable media players.

    Werner Heuser


|=| Monthly Highlights

|=| KeyTouch - configure the extra function keys of a keyboard

    KeyTouch is a program which allows you to easily configure the extra
    function keys of your keyboard. This means that you can define, for
    every individual function key, what to do if it is pressed.

    KeyTouch needs information about your keyboard model to support it. If
    your keyboard is not supported yet, you can easily get it supported.
    For this purpose keyTouch provides a simple application called
    keyTouch-editor.

    KeyTouch-editor Live is a Live CD (based on Knoppix) containing
    keyTouch-editor. You put this CD-ROM into your friends laptop and
    create a keyboard file for his or her keyboard, without having to
    install Linux. You can help the keyTouch project by creating
    keyboard files with this CD-ROM and sending them to
    marvinr(at)users.sf.net.

    [1] http://keytouch.sourceforge.net/


