I'm pleased to announce that www.storkyak.com has been up now for two
months and is gaining wider popularity.  storkyak is a blog dedicated
to developing on Linux.  It began as my sounding board as I learn to
develop more on more on Linux.

Topics covered recently include:

Getting used to KDevelop for Visual Studio users
Installing Linux on a dual opteron
Getting sensors to work on a Tyan dual Opteron mobo
Several open/gl tutorials (I'm teaching myself openg/l)
Using Linux to serve Windows and Mac clients
A few tidbits about Bash.

My blog is free from political ranting, largely because I'm sick of it,
and is entirely focused on sharing everything I learn as I delve deeper
into Linux.  Stop by and check it out!

http://www.storkyak.com

